          "what": "Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills is a structured library of 754 cybersecurity skills for AI agents, mapped to five major frameworks including MITRE ATT&CK and NIST CSF 2.0. Its key innovation is the agentskills.io standard, which defines skills as composable, framework-aligned capabilities that agents can execute autonomously. Practitioners can integrate it with Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, or 20+ other platforms to automate tasks like incident response, malware analysis, or cloud security audits, making it a practical toolkit for AI-driven security operations.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/mukul975/Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
