      "summaries": {
        "en": "magic-trace is a high-resolution tracing tool that captures and visualizes exactly what a process is doing, down to individual instructions. It uses Intel Processor Trace (PT) to record execution with minimal overhead, then reconstructs the timeline for deep performance analysis. Unlike traditional profilers, it shows every function call and context switch. You can attach it to a running process or start a new one, then inspect the trace in a browser-based viewer. Ideal for debugging latency spikes, understanding complex code paths, or optimizing low-level performance.",
        "zh": "magic-trace 是一款基于 Intel Processor Trace (PT) 技术的高精度追踪工具，能以极低开销捕获并可视化进程执行的每一条指令。它重建完整时间线，展示每次函数调用与上下文切换，支持附加到运行中进程或启动新进程。通过浏览器查看器呈现直观时序图，适用于调试延迟尖峰、分析复杂代码路径及优化底层性能，是系统级调优的有效工具。",
        "es": "magic-trace is a high-resolution tracing tool that captures and visualizes exactly what a process is doing, down to individual instructions. It uses Intel Processor Trace (PT) to record execution with minimal overhead, then reconstructs the timeline for deep performance analysis. Unlike traditional profilers, it shows every function call and context switch. You can attach it to a running process or start a new one, then inspect the trace in a browser-based viewer. Ideal for debugging latency spikes, understanding complex code paths, or optimizing low-level performance.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "magic-trace stands out for intel, introspection, and performance-tools in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "magic-trace is a high-resolution tracing tool that captures and visualizes exactly what a process is doing, down to individual instructions. It uses Intel Processor Trace (PT) to record execution with minimal overhead, then reconstructs the timeline for deep performance analysis. Unlike traditional profilers, it shows every function call and context switch. You can attach it to a running process or start a new one, then inspect the trace in a browser-based viewer. Ideal for debugging latency spikes, understanding complex code paths, or optimizing low-level performance.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/janestreet/magic-trace for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
